      "html_url": "https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec/pull/4495",
      "title": "Fix obfuscator prng",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/buixor",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec/pull/4495",
      "body": "wazero's own config.go:651-652 docs are explicit:\r\n\r\n> WithRandSource configures a source of random bytes. Defaults to return a deterministic source. You might override this with crypto/rand.Reader.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis adds back a proper random source, else it would defeat the runtime obfuscation randomness",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec/pull/4496",
      "title": "fix js obfuscator prng",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/buixor",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec/pull/4496",
      "body": "give a proper prng to wazero, else it will defeat the js obfuscation randomness.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/wetware/pkg/issues/106",
      "title": "Use cryptographic PRNG with `WithRandSource` option",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/lthibault",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/wetware/pkg/milestone/1",
        "title": "v0.1.0",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/lthibault",
      "body": "I just realized that [`WithRandSource`](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tetratelabs/wazero#ModuleConfig) maps onto `crypto/rand`, not `math/rand`.\r\n\r\nWazero is quite strict about not letting guest code make syscalls, so the value defaults to a (deterministic) stub.  We definitely want to provide guests with crypto-grade entropy, so two questions:\r\n\r\n1. What is the benefit (if any) of providing per-instance/isolated random readers?\r\n2. If there is a benefit, how can we implement a stand-alone `io.Reader` that is suitable for crypto?  (Maybe a stream cipher seeded with `crypto/rand`?)",
        "total_count": 0,

