      "html_url": "https://github.com/redis/go-redis/pull/3819",
      "title": "replace context.TODO with context.WithTimeout in channel.initHealthCheck",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/abdellani",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/redis/go-redis/pull/3819",
      "body": "Fixes #3811\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches PubSub connection health-check and reconnection flow; incorrect timeouts or context usage could cause missed pings or reconnect churn, but the change is small and localized.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> `channel.initHealthCheck` now uses `context.WithTimeout` for periodic `Ping` (5s) and subsequent `reconnect` attempts (10s) instead of an unbounded `context.TODO()`.\n> \n> The timer stop/drain logic on ping activity was adjusted to avoid blocking on `timer.C`, preventing potential goroutine stalls during health-check resets.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 9f83adc3e10e8cafab6db7ee1aed30a06affb70f. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/go-kratos/kratos/pull/3835",
      "title": "fix(transport/grpc): apply WithTimeout to streaming RPCs, matching unary behaviour (fixes #3833)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/akpradheeph",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/go-kratos/kratos/pull/3835",
      "body": "## Problem\n\nFixes #3833.\n\n`streamClientInterceptor` ignored the `timeout` configured via `WithTimeout`, silently dropping it for all streaming RPCs. `unaryClientInterceptor` has applied `context.WithTimeout` since the interceptor was introduced; the stream counterpart was never updated to match.\n\n```go\n// Before — timeout passed to unary but NOT to streaming\nints  := []grpc.UnaryClientInterceptor{\n    unaryClientInterceptor(options.middleware, options.timeout, options.filters),  // ✅\n}\nsints := []grpc.StreamClientInterceptor{\n    streamClientInterceptor(options.streamMiddleware, options.filters),            // ❌ timeout dropped\n}\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nStreaming RPCs (server-streaming, client-streaming, bidirectional) had no bounded client-side deadline from go-kratos regardless of `WithTimeout`. When a gRPC proxy has a connection pool issue and holds the stream open, the call stalls indefinitely — whereas the same RPC as unary would be cancelled after `WithTimeout` milliseconds.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `streamClientInterceptor` now accepts `timeout time.Duration` and applies `context.WithTimeout` when `timeout > 0`\n- The `cancel` func is stored in `wrappedClientStream` and called from `RecvMsg` on the first terminal error (including `io.EOF`), releasing the context when the stream ends rather than when the interceptor returns\n- `NewClient` passes `options.timeout` to `streamClientInterceptor`\n\n## Tests\n\n`TestStreamClientInterceptorTimeout` verifies:\n- With `timeout > 0`: the stream context carries a deadline\n- With `timeout == 0`: the context is passed through unchanged\n\nAll existing `transport/grpc` tests pass. (`TestServer` failure is pre-existing on `main`.)",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Siddh2024/MicroAI-Paygate/pull/1",
      "title": "fix: handle non-positive timeout and nil cancel in RequestTimeoutMiddleware",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/Siddh2024",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/Siddh2024/MicroAI-Paygate/pull/1",
      "body": "## Fixes AnkanMisra/MicroAI-Paygate#196\n\n**Bug 1 — Immediate cancellation with timeout <= 0:**\ncontext.WithTimeout with a non-positive duration creates an already-expired context, cancelling every request immediately.\n\n**Bug 2 — nil cancel causes panic in defer cancel():**\nWhen an earlier deadline is shorter than desired, cancel was left nil. The nil guard was fragile.\n\n**Fix:** Both paths assign cancel = func(){} and the nil guard is removed.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/deepshekhardas/rudder-server/pull/8",
      "title": "fix(webhook): use gateway request context for transformer adapter timeout",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/deepshekhardas",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/deepshekhardas/rudder-server/pull/8",
      "body": "## Description\n- Replace manual context.WithTimeout with req.request.Context() in batchTransformLoop\n- Remove the TODO comment about timeout handler\n\n## Changes\n- gateway/webhook/webhook.go: +6/-4 lines\n\n## Related Issue\nCloses #6839\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n---\n## Summary by cubic\nUse the gateway request context for the webhook transformer adapter so cancellations and timeouts propagate correctly per HTTP request. This prevents lingering transformations and double timeouts during batch webhook processing.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Replaced manual `context.WithTimeout` with the request’s context in `batchTransformLoop` for `gateway/webhook`.\n  - Removed the outdated TODO about adding a timeout handler.\n\n<sup>Written for commit 8b4a93f37b376cd1ccd0397d66064878e72b7681. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\n\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/cloudamqp/terraform-provider-cloudamqp/issues/506",
      "title": "Framework: Migrate batch 2, sleep/timeout polling resources/data sources",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/tbroden84",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/cloudamqp/terraform-provider-cloudamqp/milestone/7",
        "title": "M1 - Migrate all resources/data sources to Framework",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/tbroden84",
      "body": "Migrate resources that use `callWithRetry`/sleep polling from SDK v2 to Framework.\n\nResources:\n- [ ] `cloudamqp_extra_disk_size`\n- [ ] `cloudamqp_plugin`\n- [ ] `cloudamqp_plugin_community`\n- [x] `cloudamqp_security_firewall`\n\nData sources:\n- [ ] `cloudamqp_alarms`\n- [ ] `cloudamqp_plugins`\n- [ ] `cloudamqp_plugins_community`\n\nChecklist:\n- [x] Add `DeprecationMessage` to `cloudamqp_alarm` data source pointing to `cloudamqp_alarms`\n- [ ] Move `context.WithTimeout` to CRUD methods\n- [ ] Fix `context.WithTimeout` in `disk.go` API layer (remove from API, belongs in resource)\n- [ ] Fix `context.WithTimeout` in `vpc_gcp_peering.go` API layer\n- [ ] Remove from SDK v2 `ResourcesMap`, add to Framework `Resources()`\n- [ ] Remove from SDK v2 `DataSourcesMap`, add to Framework `DataSources()`",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Yoichi-Maribao/go-todo/issues/7",
      "title": "Step 6: context対応を導入する",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/Yoichi-Maribao",
      "body": "## 方針\n\n機能追加はしない。GoのHTTPリクエストとDB処理の文脈をつなげる。\n\n## 対象\n\n- QueryContext\n- QueryRowContext\n- ExecContext\n- context.WithTimeout\n\n## ゴール\n\n- リクエストキャンセルをDB処理へ伝播できる\n- DBアクセスがcontext対応している\n\n## 完了条件\n\n- [ ] DB操作が `r.Context()` を利用している\n- [ ] QueryContext系APIを利用している\n- [ ] 必要箇所で `context.WithTimeout` を使っている\n- [ ] `defer cancel()` を忘れていない\n- [ ] 機能追加をしていない\n",
        "total_count": 0,
          "html_url": "https://github.com/openai",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/smeinecke/cycletls_python/pull/31",
      "title": "fix: enforce request timeouts to prevent indefinite hangs",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/smeinecke",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/smeinecke/cycletls_python/pull/31",
      "body": "- Use context.WithTimeout instead of WithCancel in processRequest so the deadline auto-cancels when timeout expires.\r\n- Apply same timeout context in CycleTLS.Do() for direct calls.\r\n- Add ResponseHeaderTimeout and TLSHandshakeTimeout to HTTP transport so stalled proxies/servers don't block forever.\r\n- Check cached connection aliveness before reuse in dialTLS to avoid reusing dead connections that cause hangs.\r\n\r\nFixes requests hanging despite timeout parameter being passed.\r\n",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Bofry/lib-postgres-stream/pull/2",
      "title": "Fix context cancellation leaks in consumer polling worker",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/yshengliao",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/Bofry/lib-postgres-stream/pull/2",
      "body": "## Summary\nThis PR fixes context cancellation leaks by properly calling `cancel()` on contexts created with `context.WithTimeout()`. Additionally, it updates Go version requirements and dependencies to more recent versions.\n\n## Key Changes\n- **consumerPollingWorker.go**: Fixed context leak by capturing and deferring the cancel function from `context.WithTimeout()` before waiting on `ctx.Done()`\n- **consumer_test.go**: Fixed context leak in test by capturing the cancel function and deferring its call\n- **go.mod**: Updated Go version from 1.21 to 1.25.0 and updated dependencies:\n  - `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5` from v5.7.1 to v5.9.0\n  - OpenTelemetry packages to v1.43.0\n  - Various indirect dependencies to their latest versions\n\n## Implementation Details\nThe context cancellation fixes ensure that resources associated with the timeout contexts are properly released. Previously, the cancel functions were being discarded (using `_`), which could lead to resource leaks. Now they are properly captured and called to clean up the context's internal state.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011w4atyCxeMXgBSt6gfAiJS",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/dotandev/hintents/issues/1414",
      "title": "Use context timeouts in tokenflow tests",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/dotandev",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/emickwrld",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/emickwrld",
      "body": "The tokenflow tests don't enforce timeouts on RPC calls. Pass a `context.WithTimeout` to prevent hanging tests.\n\n**Files to change:**\n`internal/tokenflow/tokenflow_test.go`",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/jzakka/fugue/pull/678",
      "title": "chore(loop): cycle 268 Discovery — 동시성 area 6 sub-surface 폐기",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jzakka",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jzakka/fugue/pull/678",
      "body": "## 요약\n동시성 area cycle 262 이후 6 cycle 미방문, 29 round 적격. 6 sub-surface 새 시각 측정 모두 폐기.\n\n## 측정 (동시성)\n- A. sync.Map prod 0 — 의식적 minimal (Mutex+map 또는 미채택)\n- B. atomic.* prod 14 — counter/flag baseline\n- C. errgroup 0 — std goroutine+WaitGroup+channel 표준\n- D. context.WithTimeout/Deadline 4 — sparse 의식적\n- E. select { 6 — context cancel pattern\n- F. sync.Once 0 — lazy init 미채택\n\n## 판정\n모두 의식적 minimal / Go std 정합 → 후보 0건.\n\n## 영향 범위\nbacklog/anti-patterns 무변경. decision-log 1 entry. 동시성 area 29 round 누적 baseline.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/optiqor/kerno/issues/113",
      "title": "fix(ai): provider HTTP clients have no request timeout",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/btwshivam",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/sonusharma6-dsa",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/sonusharma6-dsa",
      "body": "all three ai providers build `&http.Client{}` with no `Timeout` (`internal/ai/anthropic.go:57`, `internal/ai/openai.go:56`, `internal/ai/ollama.go:54`). the only deadline is whatever `ctx` carries, and the analyzer never wraps a per-call `context.WithTimeout`.\n\n`engine.go` passes the parent ctx straight into `Analyze`. if that ctx has no deadline (continuous mode, or a long-lived run), a stalled TLS connect or a server that accepts but never responds blocks the whole doctor cycle forever. CLAUDE.md invariant 3 requires graceful degradation when a provider is unreachable, and this defeats it.\n\nset `http.Client{Timeout: ...}` from the configured value, or enforce a per-request `context.WithTimeout` in `DefaultAnalyzer.Analyze` before the provider call.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/AnkanMisra/MicroAI-Paygate/pull/197",
      "title": "fix: handle non-positive timeout and nil cancel in RequestTimeoutMiddleware",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/Siddh2024",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/Siddh2024",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/Siddh2024",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/AnkanMisra/MicroAI-Paygate/pull/197",
      "body": "## Fixes #196\n\n**Bug 1 — Immediate cancellation with timeout <= 0:**\ncontext.WithTimeout with a non-positive duration creates an already-expired context, cancelling every request immediately.\n\n**Bug 2 — nil cancel causes panic in defer cancel():**\nWhen an earlier deadline is shorter than desired, cancel was left nil. The nil guard was fragile.\n\n**Fix:** Both paths assign cancel = func(){} and the nil guard is removed.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n## Bug Fixes\n* Improved request timeout middleware reliability to properly handle edge cases and prevent potential issues with timeout cancellation logic.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
        "total_count": 1,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/pull/2855",
      "title": "fix(mcp): add per-tool-call timeout to prevent indefinite hangs",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/ehdwn1991",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush/pull/2855",
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add configurable per-tool-call timeout (default 120s) to prevent Crush from hanging indefinitely when MCP stdio servers block on large payloads\n- Introduce `tool_timeout` field in MCP config for per-server customization\n- Wrap `c.CallTool()` with `context.WithTimeout` in `RunTool()`\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen an LLM generates a `write_file` tool call with large content (15KB+), the MCP stdio pipe can block and Crush hangs indefinitely. Session creation and ping have timeouts (default 15s), but `RunTool()` calls `c.CallTool(ctx, ...)` with no timeout — if the stdio pipe blocks, there is no recovery path.\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|:---|:---|\n| `internal/config/config.go` | Add `ToolTimeout` field to `MCPConfig` |\n| `internal/agent/tools/mcp/init.go` | Add `mcpToolTimeout()` helper (default 120s) |\n| `internal/agent/tools/mcp/tools.go` | Wrap `c.CallTool()` with `context.WithTimeout` |\n\n## Config Example\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcp\": {\n    \"filesystem\": {\n      \"type\": \"stdio\",\n      \"command\": \"mcp-server-filesystem\",\n      \"args\": [\"/Users/me\"],\n      \"tool_timeout\": 120\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Verify normal tool calls still work within timeout\n- [ ] Verify large write_file (15KB+) returns timeout error instead of hanging\n- [ ] Verify `tool_timeout` config is respected per MCP server\n- [ ] Verify default 120s applies when `tool_timeout` is omitted\n\nFixes #2854\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra/pull/2753",
      "title": "feat(api): add per-call timeouts for redis backend operations (ENG-4060)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jakubno",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra/pull/2753",
      "body": "Wrap every redis call in packages/api/internal/sandbox with a context.WithTimeout(ctx, 5s) so a stuck redis round trip cannot block callers (e.g. while holding a distributed lock) indefinitely.\r\n\r\nSites left unchanged: lock.Obtain (already bounded by caller timeout), lock publishReleaseNotification (own 5s timeout), and the long-lived subscription manager pubsub Subscribe.",
        "total_count": 1,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/TeoSlayer/pilotprotocol/pull/202",
      "title": "fix(daemon): add 5s timeout to SubManagedCycle IPC handler (PILOT-309)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/matthew-pilot",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/TeoSlayer/pilotprotocol/pull/202",
      "body": "## What\n\nThe `SubManagedCycle` IPC handler called `ForceCycle()` synchronously, which chains through `runCycle → fetchMembers → ListNodes` — a network call to the registry with no timeout. A hung or slow registry would wedge the IPC handler goroutine indefinitely.\n\n## Fix\n\nWrap the `ForceCycle` call in a background goroutine with a 5-second `context.WithTimeout`. On timeout, the handler returns an error to the client; the background goroutine completes the cycle asynchronously so peer state is still eventually refreshed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` ✅\n- `go vet ./...` ✅\n- `go test -parallel 4 -count=1 -timeout 900s ./pkg/daemon/` ✅ (58.9s, all pass)\n\n## Scope\n\n- **1 file, +23/-6** — small tier\n\nCloses [PILOT-309](https://vulturelabs.atlassian.net/browse/PILOT-309)",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/ionutale/galaxy-empire-golang-enterprise-golang/issues/351",
      "title": "[#338] [HIGH] Background workers use context.Background() — no deadline",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/ionutale",
      "body": "Part of #13\n\n**Severity:** HIGH\n**Finding:** #338\n\n**Area:** Cross-Cutting\n**File:** `All services`\n\n**Fix:** Pass `context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 30*time.Second)` to each processing cycle in every background worker.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/kdobmayer/kond-test-go-cli/pull/37",
      "title": "Add step-level timeout enforcement to pipeline executor",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/kdobmayer",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/kdobmayer/kond-test-go-cli/pull/37",
      "body": "Implement context.WithTimeout for enforcing step-level execution timeouts in the pipeline executor. This ensures long-running steps are properly canceled and prevents pipeline hangs. Adds comprehensive test coverage for timeout enforcement across various scenarios.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/McBrideMusings/wtree/issues/83",
      "title": "fetchStatus shares one 3s timeout across status + diff — diff silently dropped on slow worktrees",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/McBrideMusings",
      "body": "## Problem\n\n`fetchStatus` runs `git status --porcelain` and `git diff HEAD --numstat` sequentially under a single `context.WithTimeout(parent, 3*time.Second)`. On a large or slow worktree, if `status` consumes most of the budget, the diff call silently times out and returns `\"\"` — the row then shows `~N files` with no `+/-` stat, which looks indistinguishable from a branch that has only untracked files.\n\n`internal/picker/picker.go` — the single `context.WithTimeout` at line 183 is shared across both calls.\n\n## Fix\n\nGive each command its own sub-timeout (e.g. 1.5s each), or run them concurrently with `errgroup` and a shared 3s deadline. Either approach ensures one slow command doesn't silently starve the other.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pilot-protocol/common/pull/13",
      "title": "fix(coreapi): per-plugin Stop timeout in StopAll (PILOT-319)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/matthew-pilot",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/pilot-protocol/common/pull/13",
      "body": "## What\n\n`StopAll` was passing the same parent context to every plugin `Stop` call. A single hung plugin would block all remaining plugins from shutting down.\n\n## Why\n\nPer-plugin `context.WithTimeout(ctx, 5*time.Second)` ensures each plugin gets its own 5-second deadline. If a plugin exceeds it, `context.DeadlineExceeded` is surfaced as a Stop error, the error is collected, and subsequent plugins continue shutting down.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — passes\n- `go vet ./...` — clean\n- `go test ./...` — all 13 packages green\n- Added `TestServiceRegistry_StopAllTimingOutHangingPlugin` that verifies a hanging plugin times out and later-ordered services still stop\n\nCloses [PILOT-319](https://vulturelabs.atlassian.net/browse/PILOT-319)",
        "total_count": 0,

