.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer changes</summary>\n<p>This version was pushed to npm by <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/~packy-anthropic\">packy-anthropic</a>, a new releaser for <code>@​anthropic-ai/sdk</code> since your current version.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@arethetypeswrong/cli` from 0.17.4 to 0.18.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/arethetypeswrong/arethetypeswrong.github.io/releases\">@​arethetypeswrong/cli's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>@​arethetypeswrong/cli</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.1</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [a4dc8a6]\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​arethetypeswrong/core</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.1</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><code>@​arethetypeswrong/cli</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.0</h2>\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>5dd9c0b: Requiring Node.js 20 for using latest lru-cache.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [5dd9c0b]\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​arethetypeswrong/core</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.0</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/arethetypeswrong/arethetypeswrong.github.io/blob/main/packages/cli/CHANGELOG.md\">@​arethetypeswrong/cli's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.18.2</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [58dca0c]\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​arethetypeswrong/core</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.2</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.18.1</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [a4dc8a6]\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​arethetypeswrong/core</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.1</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.18.0</h2>\n<h3>Minor Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>5dd9c0b: Requiring Node.js 20 for using latest lru-cache.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated dependencies [5dd9c0b]\n<ul>\n<li><code>@​arethetypeswrong/core</code><a href=\"https://github.com/0\"><code>@​0</code></a>.18.0</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/arethetypeswrong/arethetypeswrong.github.io/commits/HEAD/packages/cli\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@langchain/core` from 1.1.46 to 1.1.47\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/releases\">@​langchain/core's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>@​langchain/core</code><a href=\"https://github.com/1\"><code>@​1</code></a>.1.47</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/pull/10906\">#10906</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/f61b3450f275831e47e69c08899b4a2b67b4bdb3\"><code>f61b345</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/hntrl\"><code>@​hntrl</code></a>! - feat(core): add uuid v6 utility support</p>\n<p>Add <code>v6</code> UUID generation support to <code>@langchain/core/utils/uuid</code> by vendoring the upstream uuidjs <code>v6</code> implementation and its <code>v1ToV6</code> helper, exporting <code>v6</code> from the UUID utils index, and adding tests for deterministic generation, buffer/offset behavior, validation/versioning, and ordering.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/pull/10872\">#10872</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/a64007997a4940f51bba3c1c83dae89d1ccfb692\"><code>a640079</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/hntrl\"><code>@​hntrl</code></a>! - chore(deps): remove redundant <code>@​types/uuid</code> declarations</p>\n<p>Remove <code>@types/uuid</code> from package manifests that rely on <code>@langchain/core/utils/uuid</code> or do not require uuid type stubs directly, and refresh the lockfile entries accordingly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/pull/10792\">#10792</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/3682268cd1844b2573b01f07bee367e21cb7bdc7\"><code>3682268</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/Genmin\"><code>@​Genmin</code></a>! - fix(core): apply v1 message casting after implicit streaming aggregation</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/pull/10901\">#10901</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/f26fc4a6f461d6d0f86d59bd00197ad510432c4a\"><code>f26fc4a</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/christian-bromann\"><code>@​christian-bromann</code></a>! - fix(testing): share fakeModel invocation state across bindTools instances</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/1b19e4f84d747b481879363b4884c20eb1c0f1a4\"><code>1b19e4f</code></a> chore: version packages (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10899\">#10899</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/426e3aba21016d9ee070c3d130f74ae0047c9ce5\"><code>426e3ab</code></a> chore: fix uuid changeset (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10916\">#10916</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/245c98216ce4a6c4340954711a7ad60203283424\"><code>245c982</code></a> chore(deps): bump fast-xml-builder from 1.1.5 to 1.2.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10914\">#10914</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/126dac5a7a2fac5978448185893038ac8ea6d994\"><code>126dac5</code></a> chore(deps): bump brace-expansion from 5.0.5 to 5.0.6 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10912\">#10912</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/1abe24becdddce94c5bd2acfaf920b60a683f22b\"><code>1abe24b</code></a> chore(deps): bump fast-uri from 3.1.0 to 3.1.2 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10913\">#10913</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/229a7ad67b9a7ebd8df3ca451e0b8195bea0190e\"><code>229a7ad</code></a> fix(openai): preserve v1 assistant tool calls (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10902\">#10902</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/f26fc4a6f461d6d0f86d59bd00197ad510432c4a\"><code>f26fc4a</code></a> fix(core): share fakeModel invocation state across bindTools instances (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10901\">#10901</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/a0cd7477e59677c8d15e0e70b374afa0a2410582\"><code>a0cd747</code></a> chore(deps): bump fast-xml-builder from 1.1.5 to 1.1.9 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10910\">#10910</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/b208e625865fc7487876b652f479dbf854263e68\"><code>b208e62</code></a> chore(deps): bump ip-address from 10.1.0 to 10.2.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10909\">#10909</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/commit/f7e50fb8b98bd9969c0f5cf0967a06df15453453\"><code>f7e50fb</code></a> feat(google): Service tier and custom headers (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/issues/10704\">#10704</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchainjs/compare/@langchain/core@1.1.46...@langchain/core@1.1.47\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@openai/agents` from 0.1.11 to 0.11.4\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/releases\">@​openai/agents's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.11.4</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: avoid empty chat completions tool outputs by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1309\">openai/openai-agents-js#1309</a></li>\n<li>fix: avoid auto responses for unknown realtime tools by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1310\">openai/openai-agents-js#1310</a></li>\n<li>fix: preserve local approval rejection reasons by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1311\">openai/openai-agents-js#1311</a></li>\n<li>fix: abort active tracing exports on shutdown timeout by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1313\">openai/openai-agents-js#1313</a></li>\n<li>fix: preserve reasoning identities for OpenAI Conversations persistence by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1308\">openai/openai-agents-js#1308</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation &amp; Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: update translated document pages by <a href=\"https://github.com/github-actions\"><code>@​github-actions</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1314\">openai/openai-agents-js#1314</a></li>\n<li>chore: update versions by <a href=\"https://github.com/github-actions\"><code>@​github-actions</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1312\">openai/openai-agents-js#1312</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/compare/v0.11.3...v0.11.4\">https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/compare/v0.11.3...v0.11.4</a></p>\n<h2>v0.11.3</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: make tracing shutdown best-effort on process exit by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1306\">openai/openai-agents-js#1306</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation &amp; Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: update MCP examples by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1305\">openai/openai-agents-js#1305</a></li>\n<li>chore: update versions by <a href=\"https://github.com/github-actions\"><code>@​github-actions</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1307\">openai/openai-agents-js#1307</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/compare/v0.11.2...v0.11.3\">https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/compare/v0.11.2...v0.11.3</a></p>\n<h2>v0.11.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: add configurable sandbox archive extraction limits by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1299\">openai/openai-agents-js#1299</a></li>\n<li>fix: include structured sandbox provider error details by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1301\">openai/openai-agents-js#1301</a></li>\n<li>fix: include Cloudflare sandbox exec and cleanup error details by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1300\">openai/openai-agents-js#1300</a></li>\n<li>fix: preserve GitRepo root subpath aliases by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1294\">openai/openai-agents-js#1294</a></li>\n<li>fix: validate sandbox GitRepo subpaths by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1290\">openai/openai-agents-js#1290</a></li>\n<li>fix: guard no-op tracing span IDs by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1292\">openai/openai-agents-js#1292</a></li>\n<li>fix: add strict feature validation for chat completions by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1279\">openai/openai-agents-js#1279</a></li>\n<li>fix: keep trace batch processing alive after exporter errors by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1291\">openai/openai-agents-js#1291</a></li>\n<li>fix: drop reasoning items orphaned by dropped tool calls by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1280\">openai/openai-agents-js#1280</a></li>\n<li>fix: preserve latest response id on resume by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1281\">openai/openai-agents-js#1281</a></li>\n<li>fix: allow callback-only handoff hooks by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1283\">openai/openai-agents-js#1283</a></li>\n<li>fix: exclude computer instances from provider detection by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1284\">openai/openai-agents-js#1284</a></li>\n<li>fix: preserve output audio content from output item events (realtime) by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1287\">openai/openai-agents-js#1287</a></li>\n<li>fix: treat null audio channels as unset (realtime) by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1289\">openai/openai-agents-js#1289</a></li>\n<li>fix: align Chat Completions strict validation by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1303\">openai/openai-agents-js#1303</a></li>\n<li>fix avoid duplicating reasoning across parallel tool calls in ai-sdk by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1285\">openai/openai-agents-js#1285</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation &amp; Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: skip corrupt Prisma session records by <a href=\"https://github.com/seratch\"><code>@​seratch</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/1288\">openai/openai-agents-js#1288</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/c3437663febd8796964cada68fbe9a230907541c\"><code>c343766</code></a> chore: update versions (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1312\">#1312</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/0226da68e688762271411c9a389397b3a8709da4\"><code>0226da6</code></a> docs: update translated document pages (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1314\">#1314</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/2b4c7341575518094ab8f6978683c65f661a1c3b\"><code>2b4c734</code></a> docs: clarify how backoff.maxDelayMs works</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/087ce4b40d5e70e17019816710a13574bfadf812\"><code>087ce4b</code></a> fix: preserve reasoning identities for OpenAI Conversations persistence (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1308\">#1308</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/f36e7b2c32c7e5c825b3aa9c0a7c6c355a86f8f9\"><code>f36e7b2</code></a> fix: abort active tracing exports on shutdown timeout (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1313\">#1313</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/2c993cf0e2b9946bb386ca0fd10a705b10c0697e\"><code>2c993cf</code></a> fix: preserve local approval rejection reasons (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1311\">#1311</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/3dc9b90a79ef85cfcde3b36f0e8d2c837328da84\"><code>3dc9b90</code></a> fix: avoid auto responses for unknown realtime tools (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1310\">#1310</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/5dd3b2fa332597cb9c903525ed8aabe59a5a646e\"><code>5dd3b2f</code></a> fix: avoid empty chat completions tool outputs (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/issues/1309\">#1309</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/94f95ef5fbdbf4829f6c394e41f158ba13e0481a\"><code>94f95ef</code></a> ci: fix the post process of docs build</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/commit/4b3e3c9fea76b20ff6b5d0b68cde7875f8732309\"><code>4b3e3c9</code></a> docs: adjust the side bar</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/compare/v0.1.11...v0.11.4\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer changes</summary>\n<p>This version was pushed to npm by <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/~GitHub%20Actions\">GitHub Actions</a>, a new releaser for <code>@​openai/agents</code> since your current version.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base` from 2.7.0 to 2.7.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/releases\">@​opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.7.1</h2>\n<h2>2.7.1</h2>\n<h3>:bug: Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix(core, api): defer trace state validation. Deprecate trace state implementation in api <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/pull/6459\">#6459</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/david-luna\"><code>@​david-luna</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>important:</strong> this bug fix may be breaking for certain uses of <code>TraceState</code>\n<ul>\n<li><code>set</code> now returns the same <code>TraceState</code> instance if key/value are invalid or makes the while trace state invalid.</li>\n<li><code>unset</code> now returns the same <code>TraceState</code> instance if key is not present.</li>\n<li>best-effort parsing of invalid <code>TraceState</code>s has changed: when multiple keys with the same name are present, the most recent one will win.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>:house: Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>perf(sdk-trace-base): optimize TraceIdRatioBasedSampler performance <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/pull/6284\">#6284</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/AbhiPrasad\"><code>@​AbhiPrasad</code></a></li>\n<li>perf(sdk-metrics): reduce loop overhead in sdk hot paths <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/pull/6593\">#6593</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">@​opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.7.1</h2>\n<h3>:bug: Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix(core, api): defer trace state validation. Deprecate trace state implementation in api <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/pull/6459\">#6459</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/david-luna\"><code>@​david-luna</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>important:</strong> this bug fix may be breaking for certain uses of <code>TraceState</code>\n<ul>\n<li><code>set</code> now returns the same <code>TraceState</code> instance if key/value are invalid or makes the while trace state invalid.</li>\n<li><code>unset</code> now returns the same <code>TraceState</code> instance if key is not present.</li>\n<li>best-effort parsing of invalid <code>TraceState</code>s has changed: when multiple keys with the same name are present, the most recent one will win.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>:house: Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>perf(sdk-trace-base): optimize TraceIdRatioBasedSampler performance <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/pull/6284\">#6284</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/AbhiPrasad\"><code>@​AbhiPrasad</code></a></li>\n<li>test: test Node.js 26 in CI <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/pull/6671\">#6671</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/cjihrig\"><code>@​cjihrig</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/2400d8389a4469f7a81ccd3be2f0b2c2dd6faaf7\"><code>2400d83</code></a> chore: prepare next release (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6647\">#6647</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/f7a9b7cc854232ebf7dea2d3ec0d6adc49128f53\"><code>f7a9b7c</code></a> fix(otlp-transformer): pin protobufjs to 8.0.1 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6646\">#6646</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/cb38d7f833781c336c990757f773ce9c8360434a\"><code>cb38d7f</code></a> test(otlp-transformer): add metrics transfrom benchmark (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6628\">#6628</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/a28f12fef5fbdfb3b77a1334175b752883ef708a\"><code>a28f12f</code></a> fix(opentelemetry-core): defer tracestate vaidation (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6459\">#6459</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/b27c5146ac21deb3fb1e8fca370d34f1828f3cc6\"><code>b27c514</code></a> refactor(opentelemetry-exporter-prometheus): do not call `enforcePrometheusNa...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/a2a8186e65a04dfdaf442927fbab268076cd4f5a\"><code>a2a8186</code></a> perf(sdk-trace-base): optimize TraceIdRatioBasedSampler hex parsing (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6284\">#6284</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/4c0f3f1b911c4740a085b6c66d267bb74826b475\"><code>4c0f3f1</code></a> feat(sdk-node): set TracerProvider in startNodeSDK() (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6607\">#6607</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/417f2f17e4234417b34dbf7bdf8e24c330259dd2\"><code>417f2f1</code></a> fix(instr-xhr): do not unpatch XHR methods (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6611\">#6611</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/47ac523b124be222ac89160e4623e8a60c960f35\"><code>47ac523</code></a> Revert &quot;chore: allow browser maintainers to approve changelog edits&quot; (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/issues/6627\">#6627</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/commit/86c621d5b8344f1ecdc13a9841a90604912d0055\"><code>86c621d</code></a> fix(instrumentation-fetch): tolerate non-writable globalThis.fetch and fix pr...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-js/compare/v2.7.0...v2.7.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 20.19.39 to 25.9.1\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@vitest/coverage-v8` from 4.1.6 to 4.1.7\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases\">@​vitest/coverage-v8's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.1.7</h2>\n<h3>   🐞 Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>runner</strong>: Limit concurrency per task branch in addition to per leaf callbacks (backport)  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/hi-ogawa\"><code>@​hi-ogawa</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/10384\">vitest-dev/vitest#10384</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/4f0f2a1ee\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(4f0f2)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5>    <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/compare/v4.1.6...v4.1.7\">View changes on GitHub</a></h5>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/a09d47236e19fd3151351080c667036ca6164dc4\"><code>a09d472</code></a> chore: release v4.1.7</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commits/v4.1.7/packages/coverage-v8\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `eslint` from 9.39.4 to 10.4.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/releases\">eslint's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v10.4.0</h2>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/1a45ec596af1dd5f880e6874cb8f24dafb6a7ecf\"><code>1a45ec5</code></a> feat: check sequence expressions in <code>for-direction</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20701\">#20701</a>) (kuldeep kumar)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/450040bd89b989b3531824c6be45feb5fe3d936b\"><code>450040b</code></a> feat: add <code>includeIgnoreFile()</code> to <code>eslint/config</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20735\">#20735</a>) (Kirk Waiblinger)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/544c0c3da589166ad8e5d634f35d3d06701c57be\"><code>544c0c3</code></a> fix: escape code path DOT labels in debug output (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20866\">#20866</a>) (Pixel998)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/6799431203f2579632d0870f98ba132067f4040c\"><code>6799431</code></a> fix: update dependency <code>@​eslint/config-helpers</code> to ^0.6.0 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20850\">#20850</a>) (renovate[bot])</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/f078fef5005dceb14fc162aab7c7200e027688dd\"><code>f078fef</code></a> fix: handle non-array deprecated rule replacements (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20825\">#20825</a>) (xbinaryx)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/7e52a7151fb92eec0e0f67fe4e5ddbd1ccce796f\"><code>7e52a71</code></a> docs: add mention of <code>@eslint-react/eslint-plugin</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20869\">#20869</a>) (Pavel)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/db3468ba746407d7f286f18f7ea9db6df0e3bc08\"><code>db3468b</code></a> docs: tweak wording around ambiguous CJS-vs-ESM config (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20865\">#20865</a>) (Kirk Waiblinger)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/90846643ec6e97d447ae0d831fabe6d17b0a998a\"><code>9084664</code></a> docs: Update README (GitHub Actions Bot)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/9cc73875046e3c4b8313644cbb1e99e26b36bd3f\"><code>9cc7387</code></a> docs: Update README (GitHub Actions Bot)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/3d7b5484407403817aa9071a394d336d8ea96eb5\"><code>3d7b548</code></a> docs: Update README (GitHub Actions Bot)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/191ec3c0a3f94ce0f110df761f0b2b8949011ccb\"><code>191ec3c</code></a> docs: Update README (GitHub Actions Bot)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/6616856f28fa514a30f87b5539fc100d739a94bf\"><code>6616856</code></a> chore: upgrade knip to v6 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20875\">#20875</a>) (Pixel998)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/d13b084a3ad02f926e9addaa35fc383759ea5554\"><code>d13b084</code></a> ci: ensure auto-created PRs run CI (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20860\">#20860</a>) (lumir)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/e71c7af86dce9acc1d18cb12d2184309f6841594\"><code>e71c7af</code></a> ci: bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.5 to 6.0.7 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20862\">#20862</a>) (dependabot[bot])</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/d84393dea170f54191fd20c8268b52c81c0ccd99\"><code>d84393d</code></a> test: add unit tests for SuppressionsService.applySuppressions() (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20863\">#20863</a>) (kuldeep kumar)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/24db8cb8e6f07fba667121777a15b1785486be94\"><code>24db8cb</code></a> test: add tests for SuppressionsService.save() (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20802\">#20802</a>) (kuldeep kumar)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/2ef0549cac4a9537e4c3a26b9f3edd4c99476bf6\"><code>2ef0549</code></a> chore: update ecosystem plugins (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20857\">#20857</a>) (github-actions[bot])</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/a4297918d264d229a06cd96051ef9b91c7b86732\"><code>a429791</code></a> ci: remove <code>eslint-webpack-plugin</code> types integration test (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20668\">#20668</a>) (Milos Djermanovic)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/9e37386aa7f2ce220b2ef74a6afbac5f6b3527c5\"><code>9e37386</code></a> chore: replace <code>recast</code> with range approach in code-sample-minimizer (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20682\">#20682</a>) (Copilot)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/0dd1f9ffc9a07704d46e2a4c8d4ccc0d0908b0c0\"><code>0dd1f9f</code></a> test: disable warning for <code>vm.constants.USE_MAIN_CONTEXT_DEFAULT_LOADER</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20845\">#20845</a>) (Francesco Trotta)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/9da3c7bc92d9579f8db19ecb56e718538d09db2b\"><code>9da3c7b</code></a> refactor: remove deprecated <code>meta.language</code> and migrate <code>meta.dialects</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20716\">#20716</a>) (Pixel998)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/2099ed12a0a74c3d7f0808514362af2499b4fe2b\"><code>2099ed1</code></a> refactor: add <code>meta.defaultOptions</code> to more rules, enable linting (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20800\">#20800</a>) (xbinaryx)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/f1dfbc9ca57196de7092e1888cc99427bd6fe06e\"><code>f1dfbc9</code></a> chore: update ecosystem plugins (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20836\">#20836</a>) (github-actions[bot])</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/c75941390c14728806cd4baef4f6072f6de78318\"><code>c759413</code></a> ci: bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.3 to 6.0.5 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20843\">#20843</a>) (dependabot[bot])</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/5b817d6fdc9ae2c35b528dc662b2eca8f40f64aa\"><code>5b817d6</code></a> test: add unit tests for lib/shared/ast-utils (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20838\">#20838</a>) (kuldeep kumar)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/1c13ae3934c198c494e5958fa3a68b33244ff06a\"><code>1c13ae3</code></a> test: add unit tests for lib/shared/severity (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20835\">#20835</a>) (kuldeep kumar)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v10.3.0</h2>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/379571a975f2b24d88037b9de2e72ec61d004130\"><code>379571a</code></a> feat: add suggestions for no-unused-private-class-members (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20773\">#20773</a>) (sethamus)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/b6ae5cf07b9b51802367539cb24b245b61eaa37c\"><code>b6ae5cf</code></a> fix: handle unavailable require cache (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20812\">#20812</a>) (Simon Podlipsky)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/6fb3685bcbe9a6f72fd7dfb9129686b6fb96b0bd\"><code>6fb3685</code></a> fix: rule suggestions cause continuation in class body (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20787\">#20787</a>) (Milos Djermanovic)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/32cc7ab4ec653ce89da92deb5c40a9f4fc707fe5\"><code>32cc7ab</code></a> docs: fix typos in docs and comments (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20809\">#20809</a>) (Tanuj Kanti)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/7f479376a2fa463d823ab762db6bb37ce8d2ee8f\"><code>7f47937</code></a> docs: Update README (GitHub Actions Bot)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Chores</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/d32235ec19ceea211fa86452afa383ca05f5c2f9\"><code>d32235e</code></a> ci: use pnpm in <code>eslint-flat-config-utils</code> type integration test (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20826\">#20826</a>) (Francesco Trotta)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/3ffb14ea517de750ed1181579ef844af342e4096\"><code>3ffb14e</code></a> chore: clean up typos in comments and JSDoc (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20821\">#20821</a>) (Pixel998)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/452c4010c07dc2e36fe6ec6a8c48298878e86887\"><code>452c401</code></a> 10.4.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/b6417e8b55c9525070d6e168b485ce6ff21688ed\"><code>b6417e8</code></a> Build: changelog update for 10.4.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/6616856f28fa514a30f87b5539fc100d739a94bf\"><code>6616856</code></a> chore: upgrade knip to v6 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20875\">#20875</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/d13b084a3ad02f926e9addaa35fc383759ea5554\"><code>d13b084</code></a> ci: ensure auto-created PRs run CI (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20860\">#20860</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/7e52a7151fb92eec0e0f67fe4e5ddbd1ccce796f\"><code>7e52a71</code></a> docs: add mention of <code>@eslint-react/eslint-plugin</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20869\">#20869</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/e71c7af86dce9acc1d18cb12d2184309f6841594\"><code>e71c7af</code></a> ci: bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.5 to 6.0.7 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20862\">#20862</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/544c0c3da589166ad8e5d634f35d3d06701c57be\"><code>544c0c3</code></a> fix: escape code path DOT labels in debug output (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20866\">#20866</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/db3468ba746407d7f286f18f7ea9db6df0e3bc08\"><code>db3468b</code></a> docs: tweak wording around ambiguous CJS-vs-ESM config (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20865\">#20865</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/d84393dea170f54191fd20c8268b52c81c0ccd99\"><code>d84393d</code></a> test: add unit tests for SuppressionsService.applySuppressions() (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/20863\">#20863</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/90846643ec6e97d447ae0d831fabe6d17b0a998a\"><code>9084664</code></a> docs: Update README</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/compare/v9.39.4...v10.4.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `eslint-plugin-jsdoc` from 50.8.0 to 63.0.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc/releases\">eslint-plugin-jsdoc's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v63.0.0</h2>\n<h1><a href=\"https://github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc/compare/v62.9.0...v63.0.0\">63.0.0</a> (2026-05-20)</h1>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>require-throws</code>:</strong> avoid skipping constructors; fixes <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc/issues/1692\">#1692</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc/commit/cacb73e06a76283d9b5a96c6fdc575a89f0f26cd\">cacb73e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>chore</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>test Node 26; drop 20 (<a href=\"https://github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc/commit/c43043a2f563cf60f04baf17564de2605c1f3560\">c43043a</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>BREAKING CHANGES</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Drop Node 20</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v62.9.0</h2>\n<h1><a href=\"https://github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc/compare/v62.8.1...v62.9.0\">62.9.0</a> (2026-0...\n\n_Description has been truncated_",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/adhithyan15/coding-adventures/pull/587",
      "title": "feat(wasm-runtime): WASI Tier 3 — args, environ, clock, random, sched_yield (Go)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/adhithyan15",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/adhithyan15/coding-adventures/pull/587",
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Implements 8 new WASI Tier 3 host functions in the Go `wasm-runtime` package, replacing ENOSYS stubs with real implementations\n- Adds `WasiClock` and `WasiRandom` interfaces with `SystemClock{}` / `SystemRandom{}` production implementations and injectable fakes for deterministic tests\n- Adds `WasiConfig` struct + `NewWasiStubFromConfig` constructor for clean dependency injection; existing `NewWasiStub(stdout, stderr)` is fully backward-compatible\n\n## New WASI functions\n\n| Function | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `args_sizes_get` | Reports argument count and buffer size |\n| `args_get` | Writes null-terminated argv strings + pointer array to memory |\n| `environ_sizes_get` | Reports env-var count and buffer size |\n| `environ_get` | Writes null-terminated KEY=VALUE strings + pointer array |\n| `clock_res_get` | Writes clock resolution (ns) as i64 via injectable `WasiClock` |\n| `clock_time_get` | Writes current time (realtime IDs 0,2,3; monotonic ID 1) as i64 |\n| `random_get` | Fills memory with random bytes via injectable `WasiRandom` |\n| `sched_yield` | No-op (WASM is single-threaded); returns success |\n\n## Security\n\n- `random_get` caps guest-supplied `buf_len` at 64 MiB before allocating to prevent DoS via large heap allocation (LinearMemory bounds check is the authoritative guard; this is defence-in-depth)\n- `random_get` uses `crypto/rand` via `SystemRandom{}` in production\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] 11 new tests in `wasi_stub_tier3_test.go` using `FakeClock` and `FakeRandom` for deterministic assertions\n- [ ] All 38 tests pass (`go test ./... -v -cover`)\n- [ ] 91.9% statement coverage\n- [ ] `go vet ./...` clean\n- [ ] Existing `TestRuntimeSquare` and all WASI Tier 1 tests unchanged\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/liverpoolie/runno/issues/3",
      "title": "Slice 2 — Clock + Random providers",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/liverpoolie",
      "body": "## Goal\n\nWire the first two providers — `ClockProvider` and `RandomProvider` — end-to-end through the `WASIX` class. Implement `clock_time_get`, `clock_res_get`, and `random_get` in `wasix_32v1` against the raw sync interfaces introduced in Slice 1. Ship bundled `SystemClockProvider` and `SystemRandomProvider` simulations that mirror today's preview1 defaults (`Date.now()`/`performance.now()`, `crypto.getRandomValues()`), plus `FixedClockProvider` + `SeededRandomProvider` to exercise the determinism story. Hand-rolled test binaries only — the external `wasmer/tests/wasix` harness arrives in Slice 3.\n\n**Exit criteria:**\n\n- [ ] `clock_time_get`, `clock_res_get`, `random_get` in `wasix_32v1` call through to the configured provider and marshal results to guest memory. No-provider fallback invokes the system default (matches preview1 behaviour).\n- [ ] `ClockId` enum members (REALTIME, MONOTONIC, PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID, THREAD_CPUTIME_ID) defined in `wasix-32v1.ts` sufficient for this slice.\n- [ ] `SystemClockProvider`, `SystemRandomProvider`, `FixedClockProvider`, `SeededRandomProvider` exported from the package root.\n- [ ] Hand-rolled WASIX test binary calls `clock_time_get(MONOTONIC)` twice and `random_get(32 bytes)`; asserts monotonic delta > 0 and randomness is non-zero across runs.\n- [ ] Second test binary pins `FixedClockProvider(0n)` + `SeededRandomProvider(42)`; asserts byte-exact reproducibility across two runs.\n- [ ] Playwright green in chromium, firefox, webkit. No regressions in Slice 1 hello-world or existing WASI tests.\n- [ ] TypeScript + linter clean.\n- [ ] PR opened into `liverpoolie/runno:main`, linked to this issue.\n\n## Scope\n\n**New source files** (under `packages/wasi/lib/wasix/`):\n\n- `providers/system-clock.ts` — `SystemClockProvider implements ClockProvider`. `now(REALTIME)` returns `BigInt(Date.now()) * 1_000_000n`; `now(MONOTONIC)` uses `performance.now()` scaled to ns; process/thread CPU clocks fall back to monotonic (document the approximation).\n- `providers/system-random.ts` — `SystemRandomProvider implements RandomProvider`. Wraps `crypto.getRandomValues` in fixed-size chunks.\n- `providers/fixed-clock.ts` — `FixedClockProvider` with configurable epoch ns; monotonic advances by a caller-set tick per call (default `0n`).\n- `providers/seeded-random.ts` — `SeededRandomProvider` with a small deterministic PRNG (e.g. xorshift32 or sfc32). Seed in constructor.\n\n**Modified files:**\n\n- `lib/wasix/wasix.ts` — wire the three syscalls. Syscall handlers read provider from context; if unset, instantiate the system default lazily. No async anywhere.\n- `lib/wasix/wasix-context.ts` — already accepts `clock` / `random` slots (Slice 1). Keep the slots as-is; no new context fields.\n- `lib/wasix/wasix-32v1.ts` — add only the ABI constants needed for these three syscalls (ClockId enum, pointer/size conventions).\n- `lib/main.ts` — re-export the four new provider classes.\n- `src/main.ts` — attach them to `window` for Playwright tests.\n\n**Test harness / hello-world:**\n\n- `programs/wasix-clock-random/` — Rust binary using `std::time::Instant` / `getrandom` (via `cargo wasix`). Commit `.wasm` under `public/bin/tests/`.\n- `programs/wasix-deterministic/` — same shape but asserts internally against fixed outputs when run with seeded providers.\n- `tests/wasix-clock-random.spec.ts` — Playwright spec exercising both binaries across all three browsers. Mirror `tests/core.spec.ts` structure.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Filesystem providers — Slice 3.\n- External `wasmer/tests/wasix` harness — Slice 3.\n- Any async provider path — requires `WASIXWorkerHost` (Slice 4).\n- `clock_time_get` CPU-time clocks with real accounting — bundled default approximates; hosts wanting accuracy implement their own `ClockProvider`.\n- Preview1 refactor to use these providers — Slice 9.\n- TTY, threads, futex, sockets, signals, proc — later slices.\n\n## Design references\n\n- [`WASIX-PLAN.md` § Context & providers](https://github.com/liverpoolie/runno/blob/main/packages/wasi/WASIX-PLAN.md#context--providers) — `ClockProvider` / `RandomProvider` raw shapes.\n- [`WASIX-PLAN.md` § Determinism](https://github.com/liverpoolie/runno/blob/main/packages/wasi/WASIX-PLAN.md#determinism) — fixed/seeded example code; this slice ships it.\n- [`WASIX-PLAN.md` § Validation / Simulation providers](https://github.com/liverpoolie/runno/blob/main/packages/wasi/WASIX-PLAN.md#simulation-providers-ship-with-the-package) — `system-clock.ts` / `system-random.ts` live here.\n- `packages/wasi/lib/wasi/wasi.ts` — existing preview1 `clock_time_get` / `random_get` implementations; mirror memory marshalling.\n- `packages/wasi/lib/wasi/snapshot-preview1.ts` — preview1 ClockId enum for cross-reference.\n- [`wasix-org/wasix`](https://github.com/wasix-org/wasix) — ABI source of truth for `wasix_32v1` clock/random signatures.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Raw providers are **sync only**. A provider method returns a value or throws — no Promise shape.\n- Default behaviour with no provider configured must be byte-identical to today's preview1 defaults. Do not regress existing determinism characteristics.\n- Do not speculate ABI — only add constants needed to compile and pass this slice's tests.\n- `SeededRandomProvider`'s PRNG must be deterministic given the same seed across all browsers. Pick a PRNG whose spec is unambiguous (xorshift32 or sfc32 — document the choice in a header comment).\n- `FixedClockProvider`'s monotonic tick behaviour: document whether `now(MONOTONIC)` advances per call, per second of wall time, or not at all; pick one default, make it configurable.\n- Mirror the error model from the plan: a provider throwing a `WASIXError` subclass returns its `.result`; any other throw becomes `EIO` via the `debug` hook.\n- Do not touch preview1 code. Preview1 keeps its hard-coded defaults until Slice 9.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Requires: Slice 1 (skeleton + interfaces).\n- Blocks: Slice 3 (filesystem tests assume clock/random are live for timestamps).\n\n## PR workflow\n\nThis is part of a stacked PR chain. Slice N branches off the previous slice's PR branch and targets it in the PR; GitHub auto-retargets to `main` once the base PR merges.\n\n1. Branch off `wasix/slice-1-skeleton` (the previous slice's PR branch) — `wasix/slice-2-clock-random`. Do NOT branch off `main` until the previous slice has merged.\n2. Implement per Scope. Small, well-labelled commits.\n3. Open PR into `liverpoolie/runno:wasix/slice-1-skeleton`, linking this issue with `Closes #N`. The base will auto-retarget to `main` once the previous slice's PR merges.\n4. Wait for review on the fork side. Iterate until approved.\n5. Do **not** open the upstream PR — @taybenlor opens that once fork review is complete.\n\n## Reporting\n\nComment on this issue when:\n\n- The PR is opened (link it).\n- You hit a blocker needing a design decision — describe concretely, tag @taybenlor.\n- Review comes back; summarise what changed per round.\n",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Keats/jsonwebtoken/issues/187",
      "title": "RNG dependency injection into signature operations",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jnicholls",
      "body": "I think it would be useful for certain operations (encode, sign, etc.) to have an alternative method that accepts a `ring::rand::SecureRandom` RNG provider as an argument, or some other means to inject that dependency. Internally where an RNG is used, the crate currently creates a `SystemRandom` on demand. For cases where a different CSRNG (e.g. a different source of entropy) is deisred, or in mock testing scenarios where deterministic signature output is desired, this feature would be very useful.\r\n\r\nI don't have an opinion on the surface-level API. Perhaps `encode_with_rng` and `sign_with_rng`. For the RNG itself, it would make the most sense to create a trait owned by this crate e.g. `jsonwebtoken::crypto::Rng` w/ the same sort of interface as `ring::rand::SecureRandom`, and do a blanket `impl<R> Rng for R where R: ring::rand::SecureRandom { ... }`.",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/jbcom/paranoid-passwd/pull/1",
      "title": "feat: v3.0 — Wolfi migration, platform abstraction, full UX overhaul",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/jbdevprimary",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jbcom/paranoid-passwd/pull/1",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nComplete v3.0 migration implementing a 63-item plan across 6 pillars:\n\n### Architecture (Pillar B: C Refactor)\n- **Platform abstraction layer**: `paranoid_platform.h` with native (OpenSSL) and WASM (WASI + compact SHA-256) backends\n- **Compact SHA-256**: FIPS 180-4 reference implementation (245 lines, pure C, zero allocations)\n- **New C API**: `paranoid_generate_multiple()`, `paranoid_validate_charset()`, `paranoid_generate_constrained()`, `paranoid_check_compliance()`\n- **6 compliance frameworks**: NIST SP 800-63B, PCI DSS 4.0, HIPAA, SOC 2, GDPR/ENISA, ISO 27001\n\n### Build System (Pillar A: Infrastructure)\n- **CMake dual-target**: Native (system cc + OpenSSL) and WASM (Zig cross-compilation)\n- **melange + apko**: Wolfi package build + OCI image assembly (replaces Docker)\n- **Cosign signing**: Keyless via GitHub OIDC (Sigstore)\n\n### CI/CD (Pillar C: Pipelines)\n- **ci.yml**: 8 jobs (native tests, WASM build, E2E Playwright, CodeQL, SonarCloud, ShellCheck, hallucination check, supply chain verify)\n- **cd.yml**: Build + sign + double compilation + release-please\n- **release.yml**: Deploy signed artifacts to GitHub Pages\n\n### UX/UI (Pillar D: Overhaul)\n- Complete rewrite with dark navy (#080c14) + emerald (#34d399) theme\n- Character set builder with toggles, exclusions, custom charset\n- Multi-password generation\n- 6 compliance framework multi-select\n- 3-step wizard: Configure → Generate & Audit → Results & Password\n- Password displayed on results page with copy + 30s auto-clear\n- Real-time entropy preview\n\n### Quality (Pillar E)\n- 77/77 native tests pass (4 CTest suites)\n- 12 NIST CAVP SHA-256 test vectors\n- Frama-C annotations updated\n- All scripts pass ShellCheck\n- Hallucination detection: 8/8 checks pass\n- Supply chain verify: 9/9 checks pass\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Native tests: 77/77 pass (sha256, native, statistics, paranoid)\n- [x] WASM build: CMake + Zig cross-compilation succeeds\n- [x] Local browser test: Full audit pipeline works end-to-end\n- [x] Hallucination check: All 8 checks pass\n- [x] Supply chain verify: All 9 checks pass\n- [x] ShellCheck: All scripts pass\n- [ ] CI: Awaiting green pipeline after -mexec-model=reactor fix\n- [ ] E2E Playwright: Awaiting WASM build success in CI\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Web UI + WASM password generator with real-time 7-stage self-audit, multi-password generation, charset validation, constrained generation, and compliance checks; live audit progress and verdicts.\n\n* **Build & Infrastructure**\n  * CMake-based native/WASM builds, reproducible packaging, OCI image outputs, and deterministic build/release tooling.\n\n* **CI/CD & Testing**\n  * End-to-end Playwright tests, extensive native/WASM unit and statistical tests, and automated release workflows.\n\n* **Scripts & Tools**\n  * Supply-chain verification, hallucination checks, double-compilation and multi-party verification utilities.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Expanded docs: architecture, design, threat model, audit methodology, supply chain, security, development, and changelog.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-crypto/issues/11",
      "title": "PRG",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/jedisct1",
      "body": "The WASI crypto module requires the ability to generate random numbers.\r\n\r\nIn order to do so, WASI already provides `random_get()`, defined as a function that returns `high-quality random data`, which can be read as suitable for generating secret keys (maybe something that should be explicitly stated).\r\n\r\nNote that there are plans for that function to be in its own module: https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/master/phases/ephemeral/witx/wasi_ephemeral_random.witx\r\n\r\nShall the crypto module simply use that function?\r\n\r\nOr can you see any reason why it should use something different, or provide more options?",
        "total_count": 0,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/wazero/wazero/pull/237",
      "title": "wasi: Implement `random_get` function",
